## AI-Assisted Workflow

This repository is set up for plan-then-execute coding: Claude Opus plans each change into `PLAN.md`, a cheaper model executes it one verified step at a time, and any step that needs a decision goes back to Opus. [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) is the index of the instructions every agent follows.

| Phase | In the Claude Code panel | Permission mode |
|---|---|---|
| Plan | `/plan-feature <what to build>` (or `/plan-bugfix`, `/plan-refactor`, `/plan-tests`, …), then review `PLAN.md` | Accept edits |
| Execute | `/orchestrate-plan` | Auto |
| Re-plan one step | `/replan-step N` | Auto |
| Review | `/review-plan-diff` | Auto |

The workflow files come from a Copier template, which owns them: never edit `CLAUDE.md`, `.template/`, `.claude/commands/`, `.claude/agents/`, `.github/agents/`, `.github/prompts/`, `.github/instructions/project-template.instructions.md` or `.copier-answers.yml`. To change how agents work here, edit `AGENTS.md` or a file it lists. To pull in template improvements, run `.\.template\Update-Project.ps1`: it updates itself, replaces the template's files, merges template changes into the shared settings files, and never touches `AGENTS.md` or this README.
